  "services": {
    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The Rick and Morty Soundtrack, released on September 28, 2018, is a double album featuring music from the critically acclaimed animated series. Compiled by Sub Pop and [adult swim], the album showcases the eclectic musical style of the show, blending original compositions by series composer Ryan Elder with tracks from artists such as Chaos Chaos, Blonde Redhead, Mazzy Star, and Belly. The soundtrack also includes two new songs inspired by the show, contributed by Chad VanGaalen and clipping. The music ranges from quirky, synth-driven themes and experimental instrumentals to dream pop and alternative rock, reflecting the show’s surreal humor and genre-bending storytelling.\n\nAs a Stage & Screen release, the album stands as a unique entry in the discographies of both Sub Pop and [adult swim], bridging the worlds of television and independent music. It captures the show’s offbeat tone and emotional depth, serving as both a companion to the series and a standalone listening experience. The soundtrack was well-received for its creative curation and its ability to translate the show’s chaotic energy into a cohesive musical journey. Commercially, it was available in multiple formats, including CD, double LP on colored vinyl, and digital, with a deluxe box set following later in 2018.",
      "generated_at": "2025-11-27T13:58:16.751533",
      "model": "sonar",
      "source": "perplexity"
    }
